import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 922 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 21 | Constitutional Status of the Lin Hao Route","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 922 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 21 | Constitutional Status of the Lin Hao Route","no":922,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 21","Lin Hao Route","Constitutional Status","Personal Path"],"related":["95-Key Figures and Organizations","51-Human-Race Positioning and Traits","04-Anti-Predationism Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0922_模块5-第二十一条-林昊路线宪法地位.md","filePath":"en/0922_模块5-第二十一条-林昊路线宪法地位.md"}'),n={name:"en/0922_模块5-第二十一条-林昊路线宪法地位.md"};function r(s,e,l,u,h,c){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-922-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-21-constitutional-status-of-the-lin-hao-route" tabindex="-1">Entry 922 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 21 | Constitutional Status of the Lin Hao Route <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-922-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-21-constitutional-status-of-the-lin-hao-route" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 922 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 21 | Constitutional Status of the Lin Hao Route&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 95, 51, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-why-one-person-s-route-must-be-written-into-the-charter" tabindex="-1">Introduction: why one person&#39;s route must be written into the charter <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-why-one-person-s-route-must-be-written-into-the-charter" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: why one person&#39;s route must be written into the charter&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Lin Hao is the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s iconic figure; his cultivation route (no-anchor-ring, symbiosis-as-root unique path) is the most representative personal-original route outside the 300 systems. Article 21 formally confirms the Lin Hao route&#39;s constitutional status. This looks special, but is actually necessary: if a route that opens a brand-new evolutionary possibility is not legally recognized, later generations dare not walk it; if it is deified into unquestionable oracle, it slides into personality cult. What the charter must do is both recognize its historical contribution, and place it in a legal position equal to all routes.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Key Figures and Organizations (Document 95) and the republican axiom of Myriad Races. Its jurisprudence is: the Lin Hao route&#39;s value does not lie in the name &quot;Lin Hao,&quot; but in its verifying an evolutionary possibility previously negated by old systems — without predation and without predatory soul rings, one may also reach extremely high realms. Writing it into the charter is institutionally protecting this &quot;possibility&quot; itself, not deifying some person. The law-first axiom requires: personal routes may be recorded and referenced, but may not become personal will above the laws.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-threefold-positioning-of-the-lin-hao-route" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Threefold Positioning of the Lin Hao Route <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-threefold-positioning-of-the-lin-hao-route" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Threefold Positioning of the Lin Hao Route&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 21 positions the Lin Hao route clearly:</p><ol><li><strong>Historical status</strong>: as a pioneering route verifying anti-predation feasibility and proving symbiosis may reach the sovereign, recorded in civilizational history;</li><li><strong>Legal status</strong>: as one of Myriad Ranks&#39; selectable evolutionary paths, equal with the 300 systems and the D route, not higher;</li><li><strong>Open status</strong>: the Lin Hao route&#39;s experience, insights, and technology are fully returned to the Alaya Network, open to Myriad Ranks, no private secret transmission;</li><li><strong>Non-oracle status</strong>: the Lin Hao route&#39;s specific insights may be referenced, but no individual need, nor may be forced to, imitate it; it is one path, not the only correct answer.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all cultivators studying, drawing on, or walking the Lin Hao route. It protects later generations&#39; free reference, and also prevents using the name &quot;Lin Hao inheritor&quot; to build sects, establish cults, or collect offerings. This article especially binds Lin Hao himself and his successors: they gain no privilege because of pioneering the route, and are still bound by all clauses including four-dimensional assessment, perpetual-construction duty, and contribution measurement.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Deifying the Lin Hao route into the only correct answer, using the name &quot;Lin Hao inheritor&quot; for personality cult and interest groups, sealing the route&#39;s technology from openness, or belittling other routes as &quot;unorthodox,&quot; all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: sect-like organizations are disbanded, their sealed technology forcibly opened; those using personality cult to accumulate power are pursued under undermining Myriad-Rank-republican order. The Lin Hao route being derogated or denounced as heresy is likewise corrected — its legal status is charter-protected.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: whether the Lin Hao route&#39;s technical materials are truly fully open, and whether named sects appear, are network-monitored throughout; the Anchor Supervisory Committee monitors whether anyone uses the name &quot;Lin Hao&quot; to hollow out the charter, placing an individual above the laws — precisely what the law-first axiom requires.</p><h2 id="vi-a-road-honored-but-not-deified" tabindex="-1">VI. A Road Honored But Not Deified <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-a-road-honored-but-not-deified" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. A Road Honored But Not Deified&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 21&#39;s attitude toward the Lin Hao route is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s mature sample of treating heroes. The no-ring symbiotic route Lin Hao pioneered is recorded in history, open to Myriad Ranks, for later generations&#39; reference; but it is not deified into the only correct answer; no one must imitate, much less use Lin Hao&#39;s name to establish cults and collect offerings. Lin Hao himself likewise accepts four-dimensional assessment and bears the perpetual-construction duty, no privilege because of being the pathbreaker. This both-respect-and-restraint attitude ensures civilization will remember heroes, yet not be kidnapped by them. Heroes are signposts, not shackles; the road is open; whether to walk and how to walk, Myriad Ranks choose themselves.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: a verified-feasible route if privately hoarded deprives Myriad Ranks of one more expressway; opening it is the greatest saving</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the Lin Hao route itself is living evidence of &quot;non-predation may also reach the sovereign&quot;; constitutionalizing it institutionalizes anti-predation&#39;s persuasiveness</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type protagonist routes are deified as the destined unique, others may not learn; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Lin Hao route is one equal path, Myriad Ranks may reference or not learn</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the route is open to Myriad Ranks, not Lin Hao&#39;s exclusive privilege</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: personal original routes, once charter-recognized, merge into the open system; civilization&#39;s roads grow more and more</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Lin Hao route&#39;s constitutional status is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s model for handling the &quot;hero and institution&quot; relationship. It respects the pathbreaker, yet does not deify him; it acknowledges one road&#39;s value, yet insists all roads are equal before the law. Heroes grow old; institutions endure — this is precisely what final finalization must do.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/95-关键人物与组织.html">Entry 95 · Key Figures and Organizations</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/51-人族定位与特质.html">Entry 51 · Human-Race Positioning and Traits</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predationism Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/921_模块5-第二十条-D路线人造道则魂环合法化.html">Entry 921 · Article 20 Legalization of the D-Route Human-Made Dao-Rules Soul Rings</a></li></ul>',25)])])}const m=i(n,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
